# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repo is authored on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, but parts of it are
# checked out and executed on Linux targets — the Raspberry Pi 5 camera station
# (camera_node/deploy/, added 2026-09-20) and the Arduino UNO Q's Linux side.
# Without this file, git hands those machines CRLF files, and a shell script
# with CRLF line endings fails on the first line with a bare
# "/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory" — which reads like a
# missing interpreter, not a line-ending problem, and wastes an afternoon.

# Let git decide for anything not named below.
* text=auto

# Must be LF wherever they land: executed or parsed on Linux.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf

# Must stay CRLF: Windows-only dev tooling (tools/uno_q/).
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# Never touch: binary, or line-ending-sensitive on the wire.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.wav           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.pt            binary
*.onnx          binary
*.safetensors   binary
